## Goal

After Task 03, a developer should be able to:

1. Start PostgreSQL/PostGIS using Docker Compose.
2. Start the Spring Boot backend.
3. Start the Angular frontend.
4. Open the application in a browser.
5. See a Leaflet map.
6. Draw a polygon.
7. See the calculated polygon area in km².
8. Save the polygon as an Area.
9. Refresh/reopen the application.
10. See persisted Areas loaded from PostgreSQL.
11. Pan/zoom the map and load Areas intersecting the current viewport.

This is the first usable GIS prototype.

